Z||000000||Joe4x4||05-02-2001||06:52 AM||||I think my TPS sensor is shot. I have spare <BR>one from my 4cyl , can I use that on a 6cyl?<P>Or is it time to take a trip to the junk yard? What other car`s can I take the TPS <BR>off?<P>Do not feel like spending $100 bucks.<P>------------------<BR>Need For Speed........<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/car1.gif"> ||||reg||11
Z||000001||Bob Englert||05-02-2001||08:02 AM||||They are nowhere near $100 new.  I just looked at the PartsAmerica.com site and they listed 3 brands for $50 to $65.<P>I personally would never use a junkyard sensor of any kind in my car.  You don't really have any idea if it will work.  The TPS has too great an impact on drivability not to go with a new one IMO.<P>Check with Advance Auto or AutoZone.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
